<Slide style={{ width: 1280, height: 720, background: '#0A1020', fontFamily: 'Arial', padding: '52px 60px 30px 60px', display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column' }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#4D8DFF', fontWeight: 'bold', letterSpacing: 2.2 }}>02 · QUANTITIES</Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 32, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF', lineHeight: 1.2, marginTop: 8 }}>
        Four symbols, defined before the question that uses them
    </Text>
    <Box style={{ width: 1160, height: 1, background: '#24334C', marginTop: 14 }} />

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', gap: 24, marginTop: 22 }}>
        <Box style={{ flex: 1, flexDirection: 'column', padding: '18px 22px', background: '#111B2E', border: '1px solid #24334C', borderRadius: 6 }}>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 16, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF' }}>Λ (lambda) — what the chain arm recovers</Text>
            <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'center', marginTop: 4, height: 76 }}>
                <Math latex='\Lambda \;=\; \frac{R^{2}_{\mathrm{chain}} - R^{2}_{\mathrm{unit}}}{1 - R^{2}_{\mathrm{unit}}}' width={260} color='#FFFFFF' />
            </Box>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 13, color: '#C3D0E2', lineHeight: 1.55, marginTop: 8 }}>
                <span style={{ color: '#FFB020', fontWeight: 'bold' }}>Not clipped.</span> A negative Λ is a result — the chain arm did worse on the same test rows; clipping at zero would hide that.
            </Text>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#8FA3BC', lineHeight: 1.55, marginTop: 8 }}>
                R²_unit reads the repeat unit only; R²_chain has the chain. A denominator below 0.05 is flagged unstable (23 of 40 scaling cells) — above R²_unit = 0.95 the ratio amplifies noise.
            </Text>
        </Box>

        <Box style={{ flex: 1, flexDirection: 'column', padding: '18px 22px', background: '#111B2E', border: '1px solid #24334C', borderRadius: 6 }}>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 16, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF' }}>κ (kappa) — how fast Λ moves with data</Text>
            <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'center', marginTop: 4, height: 76 }}>
                <Math latex='\kappa \;=\; \frac{d\Lambda}{d\,\log_{10} n}' width={200} color='#FFFFFF' />
            </Box>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 13, color: '#C3D0E2', lineHeight: 1.55, marginTop: 8 }}>
                <span style={{ color: '#FFB020', fontWeight: 'bold' }}>Not pooled OLS.</span> Pooled weights are Σ(x−x̄)², so the fold with the widest level span would decide the slope, not the fold with the most rows.
            </Text>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#8FA3BC', lineHeight: 1.55, marginTop: 8 }}>
                Slope per fold, then averaged. Quoted only if the span is ≥ 0.5 dex and the smallest gap between adjacent levels is ≥ 0.25 dex; otherwise the endpoint difference is reported and never called κ.
            </Text>
        </Box>
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', gap: 24, marginTop: 16 }}>
        <Box style={{ flex: 1, flexDirection: 'column', padding: '12px 18px', background: '#16233A', borderLeft: '2px solid #4D8DFF' }}>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF' }}>n — training rows, never total rows</Text>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#C3D0E2', lineHeight: 1.55, marginTop: 5 }}>
                Levels 300 / 1,000 / 3,000 / 10,000 / all 22,242. The test rows are identical at every level; only the training prefix shrinks.
                In tier 2 that is 497 / 723 training rows, although those tasks hold 711 / 1,034 rows in all.
            </Text>
        </Box>
        <Box style={{ flex: 1, flexDirection: 'column', padding: '12px 18px', background: '#16233A', borderLeft: '2px solid #4D8DFF' }}>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF' }}>n* — where the two arms cross</Text>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#C3D0E2', lineHeight: 1.55, marginTop: 5 }}>
                The row count at which ΔR² changes sign. Quoted only if the sign changes inside the observed window (Tg ≈ 56, dielectric constant ≈ 59);
                otherwise it is written as not reported. Descriptive, with no interval.
            </Text>
        </Box>
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ marginTop: 'auto', padding: '9px 16px', background: '#0E1728', border: '1px solid #24334C', borderRadius: 4 }}>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 11.5, color: '#8FA3BC', lineHeight: 1.5 }}>
            Also fixed here: ΔR² ≡ R²_chain − R²_unit, the numerator of Λ · ρ = Spearman rank correlation between Λ and the benchmark tier (H1) · dex = a log10 ratio, so 1 dex is a tenfold change.
        </Text>
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', justifyContent: 'space-between', marginTop: 10 }}>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#5E7590' }}>Group 32 · How Much Is a Chain Worth?</Text>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#5E7590' }}>3 / 17</Text>
    </Box>
</Slide>
